{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks","id":5365,"title":"101 Story Hooks","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-07T13:24:42-08:00","id":5365,"title":"101 Story Hooks","content":"I always loved these sort of threads back on the main board. So lets get one started here. I'll start!<br /> <br /> 1. The border was always unstable really, where the City met the Woods. Not politically, no, but something was lurking there. The Summer Court was always there to keep everyone safe. Now, they are gone. No warning, No bloodshed, just gone. The entire Court, gone without a trace, and with them gone, something is stirring. Something really, really big; but what could take an entire Court?<br /> <br /> 2. The Scarecrow Ministry had always been big in Salem, but this is just Madness. Ichabod had always been a bit odd, maybe a bit low on Clarity, but he was good at his job. Now though, he's gone nuts, and taken the whole damn Ministry with him, into his insane song and dance. Now, people are vanishing, and the Thorns are shifting with an almost hungry quality, and in the middle of it all, the King of Crows sits and watches. Waiting, like a carrion bird before a battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/863-doctor-lazarus","name":"Doctor Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T04:58:12-08:00","id":29836,"title":"","content":"3. The Lost Girls Motley are a legend in changeling circles. Some say that they are the greatest talecrafters the world has ever seen, others that they are so attuned to the workings of fate that they can see past, present and future all at the same time. Guy didn't think very much of those stories, right up until the three of them appeared to him in the Hedge and prophesised that he would be King of the Winter Court before the Solstice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1664-thornfield13713","name":"Thornfield13713","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-14T05:19:13-08:00","id":29844,"title":"","content":"4 - After a long battle, the king of spring has been deposed from his throne. He was abusive of moogles, forcing them to act on their true desires, cheating changeling to act on their impulses - because Spring said so.<br /> The once king has been imprisoned and rejected by the Court. But his Crown does not fade, and - even if all the Court is against him, he still has the favour of Spring. What will the Freehold do? Try to kill him, even if this may mean going against the wishes of Spring? Just wait, and put a Council, or a Fake King to rule the Court? Or try to surpass him in his quest for &quot;desire&quot;?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1304-baroqo","name":"Baroqo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T15:59:43-08:00","id":30631,"title":"","content":"5. So this month the raven population in town seems to be increasing, and just last week they started saying Nevermore when in the presence of the Lost as if they can see past the Mask.<br /> <br /> 6. Changelings know that have a doppelganger called a Fetch, but something is strange about this Freehold. For some reason there appears to be third individuals claiming the identity of the Fetchs/Lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T00:36:25-08:00","id":31528,"title":"","content":"A member of the Gentry wants to kill two birds with one stone by starting a gang war between changelings and werewolves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1477-randompaul","name":"Randompaul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T03:12:24-08:00","id":33037,"title":"","content":"8. Something sleeps underneath the main hub for this freehold's Autumn Court. It's starting to wake up.<br /> <br /> 9. Will o' the Wisps keep appearing in town.At first it was harmless, but widely talked about. It's a nice little fun thing people see. But when the Will o' the Wisps start leading people into the hedge very frequently, the news flares up on disappearances, people begin to panic at the sign of anything slightly weird. It needs to be put to an end, fast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1740-soirgriffe","name":"Soirgriffe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T07:51:37-08:00","id":33185,"title":"","content":"10. One of the hills in town seems to be moving, Legend has it it used to be a giant and it seems to be waking up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-06T01:10:13-08:00","id":43392,"title":"","content":"11. A child-like Fae has found a group in their part of the Hedge, and seems infatuated with more thematic retro video games. How will they cope in this bizarre world with its own physics and rules? And how will they escape?<br /> <br /> 12. Come one, come all, to the traveling fair! There's danger and excitement everywhere! There's room to join if you dare! Willing or not, we don't care!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1718-rurouni82","name":"rurouni82","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T02:39:20-08:00","id":47303,"title":"","content":"13. You're in a goblin market. A merchant says 'this concludes our deal.' You have no idea what he's talking about. In fact, there's a few days missing from your memory. Should you pursue the goblin, he simply says that this is exactly what you wanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T10:21:43-08:00","id":47452,"title":"","content":"14. The Lucretia club, the most elite Spring Court dining club in the city, has always been known for its exotic fares, and has formally offered an invitation to a member of the Motley, with one price; to bring them the main ingredient for the club's next anniversary meal, and they want haunch of Briarwolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/209-that-other-guy","name":"That Other Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T08:59:34-08:00","id":48210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thornfield13713</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=29836#post29836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. The Lost Girls Motley are a legend in changeling circles. Some say that they are the greatest talecrafters the world has ever seen, others that they are so attuned to the workings of fate that they can see past, present and future all at the same time. Guy didn't think very much of those stories, right up until the three of them appeared to him in the Hedge and prophesised that he would be King of the Winter Court before the Solstice.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>All hail, Macbeth</i><i>! Hail to thee, thane of Glamis!</i><br /> <i>All hail, Macbeth</i><i>! Hail to thee, thane of Cawdor!<br /> All hail, Macbeth</i><i>, thou shalt be king hereafter!</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","user":"Daydreamer","date":". 01-17-2014, 12:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T10:26:15-08:00","id":49095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quanutmshard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=47303#post47303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">13. You're in a goblin market. A merchant says 'this concludes our deal.' You have no idea what he's talking about. In fact, there's a few days missing from your memory. Should you pursue the goblin, he simply says that this is exactly what you wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is brilliant, I'm so using this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T05:17:11-08:00","id":63385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quanutmshard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=47303#post47303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">13. You're in a goblin market. A merchant says 'this concludes our deal.' You have no idea what he's talking about. In fact, there's a few days missing from your memory. Should you pursue the goblin, he simply says that this is exactly what you wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe your fetch has made a deal with that goblin and when he sees you he thinks: &quot;Oh, well, here is the boy!&quot; And then he tells you that... What could a fetch want?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/828-j7hunter","name":"j7hunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar828_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T06:29:41-08:00","id":63407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>j7hunter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=63385#post63385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Maybe your fetch has made a deal with that goblin and when he sees you he thinks: &quot;Oh, well, here is the boy!&quot; And then he tells you that... What could a fetch want?</div> </div> </div> </div> That's interesting but changelings have Meins while fetches don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-02T08:07:25-08:00","id":63435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=63407#post63407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's interesting but changelings have Meins while fetches don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>OH, you are bloody right...<br /> <br /> 15. A big boss of Autum's Court is dealing with dangerous witches/mages to improve her skills. Maybe is preparing a strike to other Court or she wants to help another changeling, but these people are very dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/828-j7hunter","name":"j7hunter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar828_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-09T17:49:12-07:00","id":87830,"title":"","content":"\u200b16. The Winter has just been crowned. As soon as the new ruler accepts his/her position, a snowstorm hits the freehold. From then on, children start going missing around town and a woman in white and a polar bear that seems to follow her around have been seen walking around the streets late at night. What the hell is going on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2480-may-higurashe","name":"May Higurashe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2480_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T16:17:28-07:00","id":98749,"title":"","content":"17. The Winter Court Darklings have been making deal with the vampires of the city, no one knows to what purpose but January is almost over and people are beginning to suspect they may intend to hold onto power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2514-cathalramone","name":"cathalramone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2514_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T08:07:55-07:00","id":177005,"title":"","content":"18) Two legendary Changelings have come to the free holds, Hanzel and Grettle. They plead for sanctuary to hide from their Handler, the Gingerbread Witch who has sent her Gingerbread Soldiers to drag them back to Arcadia! The PC's are assigned to be their bodyguards until the situation can be resolved.<br /> <br /> Grettle is a Wizened that was forced to prepare fattening meals for her brother. Hanzel is an Ogre that was forced to perform hard, manual labor for the Gingerbread Witch, only being allowed breaks to binge on his sister's meals before he was sent back to work by the merciless witch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 19) The PC's find themselves imprisoned in an arena and forced to take part in death battles for the entertainment of others. The terms are simple, they need to achieve 100 consecutive victories to win their freedom. Lose, and their winning streak is reset, forcing them to start over from number 1. Even death is no mercy, for those who are slaughtered are soon raised again by the sadistic master of these competitions! Can the PC's satisfy the conditions to escape with their lives, or will they be forced to spill each others blood for eternity? And what will the PC's do when they find themselves changing with each competition they endure?<br /> <br /> A Changeling Origin story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 06-22-2014, 05:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-22T16:27:19-07:00","id":177413,"title":"","content":"20) There's news of a new pet store opening up in the Goblin Markets close to Arcadia. Unfortunately the Summer Court has a pretty good idea of where those &quot;pets&quot; might come from. It's time for the Gentry to have their first run in with P.E.T.A and hopefully the Summer Court acquires some reinforcements for the Freehold in the process!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-28T14:12:03-07:00","id":183216,"title":"","content":"21) a true fae appears at the freehold to beg for aid. It seems that a member of the gentry somehow lured a creature into arcadia that fae magic has no power over, and it is now rampaging across Arcadia. Being half-fae, changelings are capable of traveling to arcadia, yet being half-flesh means they are able to battle the beast with more mundane methods.<br /> <br /> The thought of returning to arcadia or working for one of the true fae is insane, even by changeling standards. But the Fae claims that several of his number have been slain by this beast, and the Gentry are getting desperate. They are willing to offer nearly anything the changelings can imagine as payment, and will offer a (literally) iron-clad contract as proof of their sincerity.<br /> <br /> Do the motley let the fae enjoy their comeuppence? Or is there something they desperately desire that only a true fae could provide? Maybe they'd just like a closer look at this fae-proof beast...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T15:29:31-07:00","id":185162,"title":"","content":"22) The Summer King symbolically marries the Sea at the start of his reign every year, which is usually just an excuse for changelings to party on the shore. This year, a beatiful Fae maiden walks out of the depths and accepts the King's vows...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3316-cantshutup","name":"cantshutup","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T15:52:08-07:00","id":185168,"title":"","content":"23) The past decade or so has seen a new sort of fairytale, an evolution of the urban legend. The internet allows 'creepypastas' to go viral, surging to viral importance in a matter of days. For the Fae, who rely so much on old stories to give them life, don't know what to do with stories that are popular for a brief flash, but for those few clever enough to seize onto these new masks, there's great power to be had.<br /> <br /> Try not to think too hard about the Slenderman stabbing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T18:02:16-07:00","id":185272,"title":"","content":"24) It finally happened, the Bridge Burners successfully destroyed the last entry point to The Hedge, thus ending the Gentry's threat to humanity forever. But things go horribly wrong when Changelings begin to slowly die without their connection to Fae magic. Realizing that their powers are waning and their people dying, the Autumn Court decides they have little choice in the matter. They have to tear open a new gateway to The Hedge. But to do so, they're going to need a lot of power, and the PC's are in charge of rounding up the Glamour needed for the ritual!<br /> <br /> <br /> 25) A plague is unleashed upon the city, a plague that specifically targets non-Fae and causes death within the first year of infection. Things look grim for the city's population, until a mysterious organization shows up to quarantine the infected and get them &quot;treatment&quot;. Unfortunately the Free Holds realize that these doctors are members of the Gentry, and they're using the plague to round up large numbers of slaves!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T09:05:24-07:00","id":193682,"title":"","content":"A Loyalist Campaign<br /> <br /> 26) The PC's are all slaves to the same Keeper, and their master has given them a task, destroy the entire Free Hold of <b>-city name here-</b> so that their Keeper can lord his accomplishment over his rival Gentry. The PC's now have to figure out a way to systematically bring down a whole society of Changelings from capturing escaped slaves to slaying them for their disobedience, to spreading dissent among the ranks. If they succeed, their Keeper promises to elevate them in status among the rest of their servants. If they fail... well best not to think about that!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Villainous Campaign<br /> <br /> 27) The PC's have been friends for years now. They escaped from Arcadia together and have been in the same Motley for as long as they can recall. Over the years, their Wyrd has increased to extremely high levels (8-10) and they are at risk of ascending into True Fae. Before they leave behind the mundane world and become practical demigods, they decide they'll need servants to tend to them in Arcadia. They begin to target mortal and Lost alike, rounding them up for the trip through The Hedge. The PC's have decided that 10 slaves each would be an appropriate number before they make the trip. Needless to say, the Free Hold will absolutely not tolerate this! Can their enormous power keep them safe against an army of pissed off Changelings, or will numbers overwhelm them before they can carry out their plans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-10-2014, 12:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-10T12:19:53-07:00","id":193848,"title":"","content":"28) One urban legend - your usual slasher fare, nothing extraordinary - has warned generations of children away from a derelict part of town that the Fae love to snatch children from. It's a raging success story for the Scarecrow Ministry, right up until people end up killed the way the killer does in the stories. A manhunt begins for a Minister too far gone to his craft, but what happens when he turns up NO COPYCATS carved into his cooling corpse?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T13:44:30-07:00","id":196541,"title":"","content":"29) One of the PC's has been pledged in an arranged marriage to a member of the Gentry before she was even born, thanks to her grandparents. The first time her fiance tried to claim her, the trip through The Hedge warped her mind and left her disoriented and confused, she saw him as a monster and fled before they could be married. When her fiance tracks her down again in the mundane world, he explains how they'll live in a luxurious castle in the beautiful countryside with dozens of servants and she'll wear the finest of vestments every day. Sounds like every little girl's dream come true. Perhaps it would be if the betrothed didn't take the medieval knight act quite so seriously. Turns out he has some very old world views on the behavior of women, namely that they should be quiet, subservient, and are expected to produce heirs for their husbands. Oh and the whole &quot;punish her if she doesn't comply&quot; law, just like the ye olden times! This doesn't sit well at all with the bride to be, but can she find a loop hole and break the pledge before the day of the wedding, or will she be forced to return to Arcadia forever because of a mistake her ancestors made?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T05:46:07-07:00","id":196700,"title":"","content":"30) The PC changeling returns to the real world, to find that a fetch has replaced him.<br /> <br /> A few days later, as the PC plots dealing with the fetch, ... his father dies. Circumstances imply that this is the fetch's doing.<br /> <br /> Twist: The fetch is entirely innocent. The PC's father died of an accident. The fetch being traumatized by what he believes to be his father dying is a direct parallel to the PC's trauma of his Durance.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T09:19:05-07:00","id":196850,"title":"","content":"31) The Summer Court captured a loyalist and after a thorough interrogation, she claims she is an agent of the Bunny King. Most of the Free Holds laugh it off, as the name doesn't sound threatening at all. So then why is every Beast who resembles a bunny, hare, or rabbit in the Free Hold acting like they're about to have a heart attack if this Fae enters their territory?<br /> <br /> <br /> 32) The Autumn Court has uncovered a map which leads to the location of the legendary sword Hedge Trimmer. According to the legends, this blade allows those who wield it to pass unhindered through The Hedge. The problem is that the sword is imbedded in living rock, and only the chosen one may remove it. If the Free Holds could get their hands on that sword, it could vastly improve their ability to rescue others from the True Fae! The hunt is on to find someone worthy of removing the sword, and while they're at it, they have to cross through The Hedge to reach it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T01:11:59-07:00","id":199791,"title":"","content":"33) Feeling sympathy for the Lost who were abducted at a much younger age, the Free Holds decide to open up a &quot;private&quot; school for teaching Lost the educational material they did not have access to in Arcadia. Will this newly opened school give them some degree of normalcy in their now twisted lives, or will the pressures of school only add to their problems?<br /> <br /> A Lost Middle / High school RP","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T05:11:58-07:00","id":199901,"title":"","content":"Here's one I did a long time ago:<br /> <br /> <i>In Denver, Colorado, there exists an old church that holds a treasure like no other within its catacombs. Known as the Eternal Casket, this legendary token has been guarded by the Court of Solstice since its discovery five years ago. But it is what sleeps inside the casket that attracts changelings to the place.<br /> <br /> Her name is Emilia, or St. Emilia, as the Court of Inbetween has taken to calling her. Within the casket, she sleeps the dreamless sleep. Alive, but trapped in timelessness. Never aging, never waking. While in this state, the Fairest Bright One blesses all who look upon her with the most precious commodity a changeling can know: a sense of clarity.<br /> <br /> But not all are willing to let her remain within the casket. Despite what her guardians say about her having willingly entered the glass coffin, there are those who believe them liars, and demand her release. Others say that it is through her sacrifice that the Freehold of Denver has survived for so long, creatures of the Hedge, or even Arcadia unable to near the church because of its &quot;holy&quot; occupant. Besides, surely the needs of the many out way the needs of the few, right?<br /> <br /> Regardless of one's perspective, a hedgefire war has sprung around the Casket, one that is between the release, and protection, of St. Emilia.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T05:35:10-07:00","id":199908,"title":"","content":"35) Someone spiked the Spring Coronation\u2019s toast with a hallucinogen! Now a fairly large portion of the Freehold is tipsy and reacting to things that aren't there. Even worse, the transfer of power ceremony hasn't finished yet. If someone doesn't manage the situation soon, between the drunk/crazed fae powers running amok and the delay in the exchange, the party is going to get some attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T11:41:49-07:00","id":200286,"title":"","content":"36) King Kong, Sharktapus, Dinocrock, Tremors, the Free Holds have been encountering a lot of Fae who resemble movie monsters trying to invade their territory. The question is <i>why, and who's the one behind the operation?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-21T12:39:55-07:00","id":204098,"title":"","content":"37) Collecting figurines has been a hobby of yours, and your last purchase was from some Chinese gift shop. You bought a golden figurine of your Zodiac animal, thinking it would be pretty cool for your collection. After putting it on your bedside and going to sleep last night, you awaken to find two things amiss. One, you're inside a cold, metal cage instead of your nice warm bed. And two, you've become your Zodiac animal! Thankfully you seem to be some manner of hybrid, rather than a full beast, and therefor have access to your digits. Maybe you can open the cage from the inside out! As your senses begin to flare, the image of the store owner from yesterday appears before you, holding the figurine you bought with one hand, and stroking it with the other... &quot;Now I have the full set!&quot; he says, as you notice you're not the only cage in the room.<br /> <br /> <br /> A semi-durance story in which all the players are Beasts from one of the Chinese Zodiacs. Dragon, Goat, Rooster, Dog, Snake, Rat, Monkey, Pig, Tiger, Ox, Rabbit, Horse. Made for up to 12 players (13 including the ST)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-21-2014, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-23T16:16:34-07:00","id":206658,"title":"","content":"38) a changeling uses a goblin contract to become pregnant by her mortal husband. The process runs its course, and the resulting child is healthy and quite normal (as normal as the child of a changeling can be, of course) <br /> <br /> But things can't be that easy when goblin contracts are involved.<br /> <br /> - Since being born, there have been a half-a-dozen attempts to abduct the child. Some of the attackers were known bridge-burners, others were suspected loyalists. What could both groups possibly want a changeling child for?<br /> <br /> - the fuel for the creation of a new life came at a cost. The parents are slowly weakening, and will be dead in a matter of days unless a way to help them is found.<br /> <br /> - at the child's birth, three True Fae maidens appeared to give three 'blessings' that are predicted to cause the ruination of the freehold and all that dwell within. can you cheat fate and keep the child safe from those who'll attempt a more bloody method of stopping prophecy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1457-quanutmshard","name":"Quanutmshard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"61"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T12:44:57-07:00","id":244276,"title":"","content":"39) Its the week before Valentine's Day, a time for love and sweets. But when the Queen of Spring is delivered a human heart stuffed with chocolates, something has gone terribly wrong. It appears one of the True Fae has taken a liking to this holiday, and is trying to woo the queen to be his Valentine!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T18:51:01-07:00","id":244453,"title":"","content":"40. While trying to escape from a Gentry hunting party in in the Hedge, the Motley take a wrong turn and find themselves in the most horrifying world of all... the CWoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3738-illuminated-minutia","name":"Illuminated Minutia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3738_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T14:33:24-08:00","id":375587,"title":"","content":"41) The Queen of the Spring Court has sent you to procure a device that can translate anyone's speech pattern into the language of love. The Goblin market has such a device, but the shop keeper wants the preserved remnants of Osiris' left eyelash in exchange. Another Hobb has such an artifact, but he wants a wrought iron chastity belt. And so on, and on, and on - trade quests are bull shit!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T20:08:51-08:00","id":375796,"title":"","content":"42) Once a month, the monarchs of all the Courts have a meeting so that they're on the same page when it comes time for them to rule. You have a friend who's an assistant to one of those monarchs. This friend is very late coming back from the meeting. At first you assume that it's because something contentious came up. Then they send you this text:<br /> <br /> <i>Get out of town NOW</i><br /> <br /> If you try to call them, someone on the other end picks up, but there is only silence for a moment--and then gleeful, hysterical laughter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":233,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","user":"Daydreamer","date":". 01-20-2015, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-19T20:44:55-08:00","id":375834,"title":"","content":"43) The local Hedge, a typical maze of briar and unending foliage, has gained a new feature, seemingly overnight. One of the paths leads to an enormous pit, blocking all progress. It's deep enough that the bottom is hidden by darkness.<br /> <br /> However, a stone staircase winds down around its edge...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T08:43:31-08:00","id":377256,"title":"","content":"44) A group of hobgoblins puts out an announcement for an auction. They're selling the orphaned titles of a True Fae who was destroyed by unknown means.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/233-daydreamer","name":"Daydreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar233_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"193"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-21T13:20:51-08:00","id":377499,"title":"","content":"45) Every single dog in town is constantly howling, freaking everybody out. It goes on for three days without pause. Then the body of Loyal Chien, Summer Court Beast, shows up killed by lethal amounts of bee stings. What's going on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4722-birnam","name":"Birnam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4722_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-22T07:10:35-08:00","id":378005,"title":"","content":"46) You spot a man standing atop a bridge railing. A large black dog sits below him. As you approach, you see that the man is crying, and you can hear the dog talking to him.<br /> <br /> &quot;You're doing the right thing. You know there's no such thing as a talking dog. If you do this, you're going to save your family a lot of pain. Do you really want them to have to deal with you being in a mental hospital?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3629-bibliomancer","name":"Bibliomancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-20T06:23:49-08:00","id":412677,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:14px\">47) The yearly sacrifice, that's what it was. You grew up in a town of pagans who still adhered to old style traditions to ensure their crops grew plentiful and healthy. Whether you actually believed in their ways before, or you were skeptical, it didn't matter. The town didn't receive any tourists that year, so they were forced to select one of their own for sacrifice, that someone was you! Bound and gagged, you were handed over to whatever Fey had tricked the town into believing it was a god. After your escape, you possess the one thing that can bring the Fey's plans crashing down; knowledge of the truth. You have seen what lies on the other side, and you know this creature to be a false god, one who can be beaten!<br /> <br /> Problem is... this is the backwoods country, and it takes something really earth shaking to convince people to abandon the old ways. This Fey has been the town's food supply for centuries, and all you have are fanciful tales and heresy to counter them!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 48) Remember when you were a kid and used to play with your dinosaur toys? It sure was fun making them attack the little army figures and eat each other, wasn't it? Well if you knew then what you know now, you wouldn't have found it funny in the least! Turns out your Keeper likes playing with dinosaurs too, and has turned their realm into some kind of prehistoric savage lands! Can you escape from this jungle in time, or will you end up like so many army figures who came before you?<br /> <br /> Durance Story</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 02-26-2015, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-25T16:08:53-08:00","id":419501,"title":"","content":"49) Escapes from Arcadia rarely are peaceful affairs, but some Changelings emerge from the hedge in far worse shape then others- screaming, frothing, and dangerous. In order to better protect the secret of their existence and the safety of changeling and mortal alike, the courts in your large urban freehold have come together to create a specialized first response team of changelings tasked with making first contact with fresh escapees and subduing and stabilizing those who come out in a dangerous state. The job is risky, tricky, and often violent, exposing members to the strangest, scariest, and most tragic examples of Changeling-kind. As a member of this group, will you and your teammates succeed in helping these disoriented refugees on their first step to rejoining humanity? Do you have what it takes to face others fresh from the pain of a slavery that still dwells heavily on your own heart, perhaps bearing the scars of the same Keeper that tormented you? And what will you do about the mysterious entity that seems to be reaching your team's targets first...and leaving them stone dead as soon as they emerge?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>i don't know a hecking thing, my guy","edited":{"userid":4416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","user":"Heedra","date":". 02-25-2015, 07:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4416-heedra","name":"Heedra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-26T20:02:39-08:00","id":421089,"title":"","content":"50) It turns out your not the only one in your family tree who your Keeper fancies. For reasons beyond your comprehension, your Keeper is obsessed with your bloodline. Every 10 years or so, they return to claim another of your blood relations. Last time it was you, but you managed to escape rather than become part of whatever sick plan they had in store. This time, your Keeper has targeted the kid sister your parents conceived after your escape.<br /> <br /> If you try to save her, it will lead your Keeper straight to you. If you run and hide, you'll be condemning yet another (much younger) family member to your personal hell!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T17:21:52-07:00","id":443371,"title":"","content":"51. On the eve of an important ceremony, a high ranking member of the PC's court falls comatose. Her role is vital for the completion of the ritual. Unfortunately for the Fae, neither true love nor a simple kiss will help her regain consciousness. No indeed, it will require a long descent into the depths of dreams, ultimately using the Skein to climb up through her subsconscious and into the nightmare world she has become trapped within. Can the changelings free her by confronting whatever invaders torments her dreams, or will they find themselves likewise trapped in an endless sleep?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T19:47:34-07:00","id":443616,"title":"","content":"Inspired by events in my mortals game:<br /> <br /> 52: A new changeling has emerged from the hedge. As part of the Freehold's &quot;newbie routine,&quot; your motley is assigned to look into their old life and determine the risk of getting their original life back. Only problem is: the life that they describe doesn't exist. Are they lying about their old life, or did their keeper somehow erase them from reality?<br /> <br /> 53: While on the run from a hunter, a local changeling, let's call him Jack, opened a door to the hedge to get away. Odd thing is, the door hasn't closed. It's three days later, Jack hasn't returned yet, and there are hedge beasts finding their way through the door.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2283-andreamus","name":"andreamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2283_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-26T17:34:35-07:00","id":458504,"title":"","content":"54: It's true, the Japanese have created a form of Tofu that looks and tastes like human flesh. They brand it as a healthy alternative to cannibalism, and perhaps it is. Problem is, most people don't have a craving to eat <i>real</i> human flesh, much less an impersonation. So who is this mysterious buyer who's purchasing it in bulk on a nearly monthly basis?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T00:16:23-07:00","id":995536,"title":"","content":"(Is thread necromancy okay for hook threads like this?)<br /> <br /> 55. The Bravos, a notorious group of Changeling smugglers and Market dealers have long been known and notorious for trawling the Hedge in their mobile hollow, a gleaming UFO. But someone's finally managed to shoot them down, and they've crash-landed amidst the thorns, their valuable cargo presumably still on board. One the Hedge's biggest bounties is there for the taking, but it won't be there for long. And of course the ship itself might be the most valuable thing there- anyone who could get such a fine piece of hedgeneering up and running again would be poised to pick up where the Bravos left off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 10-30-2016, 04:35 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T01:03:09-07:00","id":995546,"title":"","content":"Wearing my recent inspirations on my sleeve for these.<br /> <br /> 56: A local student of little prior note has a surprise breakout in her new play, a fantastical opera that quickly draws large crowds to the college theater department and already threatens to become a traveling act; it is sweeping and extravagant and vivid.. and references your Keeper by name, describing their domain in exacting detail. What does it mean - and what do you do when the actors start to vanish?<br /> <br /> 57: The nearby Hedge has become increasingly unstable, with old Trods no longer proving reliable and many hobs taking on bizarre new forms. Something has warped the very fabric of the Wyrd and the world of faerie, and as many come to fear for the safety of the freehold amid such uncertainty the source of flux is discovered: a small group of passionate mortal artists creating odd works, with no knowledge of the supernatural or strange. How is there art having such a profound effect on the environment, and how will you stop them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-28T13:26:04-08:00","id":1039579,"title":"","content":"weirdly topical idea I had today.<br /> <br /> 58. The Freehold of Washington D.C. honors any presidents who happen to be a changeling by appointing them a high position in one of the seasonal courts. The current President, a fairest from new york when appointed declared himself as &quot;The All Seasons King&quot; the members of the freehold thought him mad...until the wyrd acknowledged the proclamation and gave him a crown representing all the courts. Now the members of the freehold are scrambling in all directions trying to find a way to undo whats occured or find a means of escape before the Hedge subsumes the freehold and the King becomes a member of the Gentry/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12235,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","user":"emmens","date":". 01-28-2017, 04:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12235-emmens","name":"emmens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12235_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-19T06:15:47-07:00","id":1105356,"title":"","content":"<b>&quot;UNDERSTUDY!&quot; (Durance)</b><br /> <br /> <b>59:</b> There's a new Keeper on the block and they happen to be a lover of Shakespeare's plays. Now anybody even remotely familiar with the (in)famous playwright knows that his stories are dark as shit and just as bloody. And, oh look at that, this month he wants to see the story of Hamlet; in which the vast majority of the cast dies throughout the course of the play. Even worse, you've been contracted as one of the actors! You need to find a way out of this mess before you end up impaled on a sword, or something even worse!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Laughing Pains</b><br /> <br /> <b>60:</b> You know that creepy fad on the internet where people have been dressing up like clowns and harassing the shit out of people? Well it's especially bad in your local area. These aren't just any psychotic clowns, they're Huntsmen and they're targeting the Lost in the dead of night and dragging them back to their Keepers. The worst part about their attacks is the twisted mockeries of pranks, gags and tricks they utilize for subduing members of the Freehold. Well, that and the psychotic laughter accompanying their presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 01-29-2018, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T10:23:22-07:00","id":1108816,"title":"","content":"61. There is a youtube channel that members of the freehold has stumbled across that's being filmed in your area. It is about these teens documenting themselves at first pulling a Slenderman hoax but as the footage unfolds it seems that they are actually being stalked by a being which looks remarkably supernatural and like Slenderman. Either the group of teens have a full special effects team or <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/799082-cofd-diy-mystery-cults?p=1108502#post1108502\">something's really going on</a>. A few members of the Scarecrow Ministry are suspected but then again a few of them have become paranoid shut-ins, and it is rumored they are scared of Slenderman too. Is this the work of the Gentry? Your motley has been asked to investigate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 06-29-2017, 11:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-06T14:35:51-07:00","id":1112349,"title":"","content":"<b>62:</b> A Fairest Ifrit is an extremely dangerous adversary and an invaluable ally. Their words and visage can inspire rebellions to spread across the land like wildfire, consuming all enemies in their path and laying waste to their holdings. Until recently, the Summer Court was in possession of just such a Changeling; a high ranking knight among their court. But now they've gone missing and it's becoming obvious that they aren't in the Freehold anymore. The obvious assumption is that they've been captured again, but there's no solid evidence to go by. So now your motley (along with several others), have been contacted to hunt for the lost Lost before their Keeper can turn them into a living weapon against the Freehold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T05:01:21-07:00","id":1120749,"title":"","content":"63: Twin characters are in fact changeling and fetch. The changeling was taken as a baby, but its father managed to find the captor and get the child back in exchange for his own servitude, leaving the mother alone with two babies. With a split soul, the changeling never felt like a part of the community. Now, a local witch has brewed a potion, initially for lovers, for joining souls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13128,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","user":"Spinnerling","date":". 07-26-2017, 08:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T12:18:49-07:00","id":1120944,"title":"","content":"<b>64:</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1120890#post1120890\">A local witch</a> has been baking tarts which cause the death of the first person you're thinking of when you eat it, and while it isn't a permanent way to deal with a Huntman, as they reform after being killed, there are rumors of certain unpopular changelings with dark reputations have been trading extremely unlovable human children to the witch for the tarts and basically resorting to eating a tart to escape otherwise inescapable situations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 07-26-2017, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T15:43:39-07:00","id":1121055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1120944#post1120944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>64:</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show?p=1120890#post1120890\">A local witch</a> has been baking tarts which cause the death of anyone you're thinking of when you eat it, and while it isn't a permanent way to deal with a Huntman, as they reform after being killed, there are rumors of certain unpopular changelings with dark reputations have been trading extremely unlovable human children to the witch for the tarts and basically resorting to eating a tart to escape otherwise inescapable situations.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Problem with that is a single wandering thought can have disastrous consequences. It would take a disciplined mind for those tarts to be an effective defense mechanism.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>65)</b> It Takes a Freehold<br /> <br /> Most Changelings are created through unusual circumstances, but one in particular is even stranger. Abducted by the True Fae on the very day of their birth and rescued from their Keeper almost as suddenly, this Changeling (Kith and Seeming up to the ST) has been literally raised from birth in the ways of the Fae. That makes them an invaluable asset to the community that they can't afford to lose. So far, the Freehold has honored a pact to raise the child communally without pressing their agenda on them. But now they are coming of proper age and it is time for them to decide which Court they will pledge their dedication to. They can't force the choice upon them, not without jeopardizing the child's loyalty, so they have to convince them to make the decision of their own free will.<br /> <br /> That means you get to play the role of liaison and try to show off why your court is the best choice! Oh, and if your motley is a mixed bag of courts, they've also been chosen to serve as liaisons; because Changelings can't ever have anything the easy way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-26-2017, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-26T18:17:45-07:00","id":1121119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1121055#post1121055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem with that is a single wandering thought can have disastrous consequences. It would take a disciplined mind for those tarts to be an effective defense mechanism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good point, fixing the wording to be clear, not that a stray thought idea you pointed out might not be potentially very tragic or accidentally suicidal, but right now it is unclear how many people the tart can kill, which is only one by the way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-12T14:57:54-07:00","id":1139781,"title":"","content":"67: Campaign of the King:<br /> <br /> The Courtless King, a renowned leader of the Lost and Former Duke of Summer has come to the city. He seeks enlistment for his War of Ivy, a battle stretching years through the Hedge and Briar. Supposedly, the Courtless King knows a Trod to the heartland of Arcadia itself where the First Root of the Hedge rises from the enchanted ground. Many Lost have found themselves recaptured or dead during his crusade, but somehow the Courtless King remains untouched by the ravages of war. Already some of the PC's allies have seemed swayed by the King's eloquent appeal. That very night the PC's are plagued by a dream of massacres under the shade of Hedge walls. Through the violence, the King stands impassively and watches it all, holding an aged pocket watch that ticks forward with each death on the field below. <br /> <br /> 68. The Oathsworn Dead:<br /> <br /> Long has the city remained free of the Gentry's meddling ways. Melanie May, vaunted Queen of Spring, supposedly tricked the shield of a Gentry into revealing a hidden clause of contracts she alone possesses. With this power she has united the Lost in a Grand Oath that is powerful enough to keep the Fey from ever entering the city, through dream or door. For such powerful magic, each Changeling in the city must swear into the Oath, that their own lives be forfeit if one of their own ever takes the life of another sworn and is not brought to justice. For decades this enforced peace has attracted the weary and the hunted to the relative safety of the city. But something has happened. Melanie May lays dead the eve before the celebration of her coronation, a Fae dagger planted in her breast. The sands begin to drop and each Changeling of the city can feel the magic of the Oath pressing in on their hearts. If the murderer cannot be found, it will mean the lives of each and every Changeling in the city, while the True Fae circle hungrily, their goals well within sight.<br /> <br /> <br /> 69. A Motley Coliseum:<br /> <br /> On the night of the Eclipse, The Carved Gladiator, (A Gentry of some power), enacted an ancient contract with the Moon to draw all the city into the Hedge, leaving the grandest Fetch Illusion in its place. There, trapped in the Thorns, the Lost and Mortals of the city must battle till only one team remains, for the glorious privilege of a single Wish. The Players can either be part of this battle royale, or stumble into a city of twisted twine and twigs, forced to deal with the most elaborate kidnapping that has ever yet occurred in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> 70. The Gate Below:<br /> <br /> For as long as the Lost can remember, the Courts have warred. The city has been divided into territories and there is no peace between the kings and queens that hold their power. Fate always seems to intervene to keep the Lost locked in combat. But when a hit, organized by the Summer Court, fails to slay a certain fetch, the entire city is promised deliverance from the chaos if only they deliver the Fetch to Summer's hands. The PC's discover the Fetch carrying a dangerous secret, an old oath of war for the Gate of Exits, a token powerful enough to deliver the hordes of Summer to the door of the Fey or the spies of Winter to any locked or warded room.<br /> <br /> 71. DayDream:<br /> <br /> A figure of tattered rags with an iron face has been seen in the dreams of many lately. It visits no violence, simply delivers a message that echoes hollowly through all the dreams to follow, whispers in the cracks of nightmares. &quot;Beware the Long Sleep.&quot; So far the Changelings have not been able to track down this phantom and cannot determine if it is perhaps one of the Gentry. Mortals around the city are beginning to contract fits of narcolepsy, seemingly at random, but when they awake their body is cut with thorns the Lost know all too well. As more and more seem to be succumbing longer and longer to the Sleep, the Lost find that the world around the sleepers bleed their dreams into the world around them. Can they find the cause and stop it before all is dream and none ever wake? <br /> <br /> 72. To Rewrite an Ending:<br /> <br /> The Lost have found a book. Inside, written carefully on old paper, are tales of the Motley's future and the terrible death that comes for them all. It is considered a warning first, till the events in the book start coming true, fate twisting to fulfill them even as the Motley desperately tries to stop it. Can they unwrite their destiny? Or will their blood blot the period at the end of the story?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7452-tulpa-theory","name":"Tulpa Theory","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T01:27:57-07:00","id":1139855,"title":"","content":"<b>73) A Suitable Replacement:</b><br /> <br /> The local Gentry have come to bargain with an offer that has the entire Freehold stupefied as they try to come up with a straight answer. They're offering to cease and desist any current and future attempts to recapture their escaped slaves, allowing them to live out the rest of their unnatural lives in peace. But in exchange, they demand that somebody take their places in Arcadia. It can't just be any random schmuck, either; the Gentry want a fair trade, and that means finding somebody who is capable of fulfilling the job at least as well as their escapee could, if not better.<br /> <br /> While many Changelings believe the deal is unthinkable, many others disagree. Changelings both young and old are seeing the potential benefits, with the young ones being too freshly traumatized by their escape and the old ones being too weary of a life time of constant paranoia and bloodshed. Some among the Freehold have taken to privateering, seeking out and kidnapping worthy mortals and selling them in exchange for gauranteed freedom. Are you one of these privateers, or one of the outraged Freeholders attempting to stop them from condeming others to eternal suffering?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>74) Fool's Gold:</b><br /> <br /> Somebody, somewhere, stole the wrong trinket from one of the True Fae. Upon initial inspection, it seems to be an object of immense monetary value, but it has a curse placed upon it. Anybody who gains possession over said trinket is slowly consumed by greed (at a rate of -1 permanent Willpower dot each week), to the point where they eventually descend into megalomania and will slaughter anybody over the tiniest scrap of wealth. Now, this trinket is out there somewhere in the Freehold and it's tearing the community apart as everybody seems to want to get their hands on this thing!<br /> <br /> To make matters worse, the trinket can only be destroyed by the willful actions of its current owner, which becomes increasingly more difficult the longer they are exposed to its effects. Never the less, you know what you must do. For the good of the Freehold, you must seize control of this treasure, and hopefully destroy it before its power corrupts you as well!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-14-2017, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T17:47:01-07:00","id":1140047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1139855#post1139855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>74) Fool's Gold:</b><br /> <br /> Somebody, somewhere, stole the wrong trinket from one of the True Fae. Upon initial inspection, it seems to be an object of immense monetary value, but it has a curse placed upon it. Anybody who gains possession over said trinket is slowly consumed by greed, to the point where they eventually descend into megalomania and will slaughter anybody over the tiniest scrap of wealth. Now, this trinket is out there somewhere in the Freehold and it's tearing the community apart as everybody seems to want to get their hands on this thing!<br /> <br /> To make matters worse, the trinket can only be destroyed by the willful actions of its current owner, which becomes increasingly more difficult the longer they are exposed to its effects. Never the less, you know what you must do. For the good of the Freehold, you must seize control of this treasure, and hopefully destroy it before its power corrupts you as well!</div> </div> </div> </div>Does giving into the corruption turn you into a dragon, perhaps? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>75) Lore</b><br /> <br /> &quot;Add one lore you know to this letter and send it to another person. And, do not tell others of more than ten stories written in here. Break this, and a letter with your name in it will spread. I am the dark place, the underground, and the mastermind. I am coincidence, destiny, and miracle. I am meaningless and meaningful. I am the lore. Until the day I win against fact...&quot;<br /> <br /> E-mails that start with the above paragraph, each containing a dozen or so short urban legends and creepypastas, have been circulating around the city's faerie population. Web-savvy courtiers have noticed that its a translation of something that used to be a hit in 2ch more than a decade ago, but the 'lore' contained in each mail is not like what were posted in 2ch back then. The freehold is on high alert, trying to find who or what is sending these e-mails, and if possible how to stop it.<br /> <br /> <i>Possible Scenarios</i><ul><li>The lore is a tool used by a crafty and potent Huntsman who adapted somewhat in the contemporary era. This was discovered by the motley-mates of a changeling who spread more than ten stories to see what would happen. He narrowly escaped the thing that came out of his laptop by escaping into the Hedge, and was not seen ever since. Now the changelings know just how dangerous these e-mails are, but it has already spread throughout the city. Possibly the entire country.</li> <li>Fact-checking the background of each lore reveals that they're entirely false, such as one story about 9/11 describing it as happening on 1999 instead of 2001. Exactly thirteen hours later, whoever did the fact-checking finds that the false background has become the truth, with only themselves remembering what was the truth. Even the people who know of this phenomenon are vulnerable to this change when someone else enacts it. One of the changelings propose a preposterous yet chilling analysis of what could be transpiring - the world itself is being replaced by its fetch, piece by piece.</li> <li>Changeling sorcerers have discovered that each story is an instruction that teaches Goblin Contracts, draped in elaborate symbolism and hidden behind mundane language. One problem is that it doesn't take a changeling to learn them. The more skilled and luckier mortal occultists, and even certain supernatural ones, have successfully learned these Contracts and are using them with impunity. It's only a matter of time before the goblin behind all this comes to collect all those debt in one fell swoop.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-13T22:42:20-07:00","id":1140086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1140047#post1140047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does giving into the corruption turn you into a dragon, perhaps? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Who's to say? Also, I meant to go back and edit in the corruption manifests in the form of losing 1 permanent Willpower each week, but I forgot about it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>76)</b> <b>Satyriasis</b><br /> <br /> The King of Spring has a sensitive, personal matter he's been requesting your motley's help with. Over the last couple of years, he's had trouble... performing, as it were. Not trusting mortal medicine to work on his supernatural physiology, he decided to hit up the Goblin Markets and see if they had anything that could restore his virility. It turns out they did, and within a few minutes, the King of Spring had his hands on a new form of male enhancement supplement brewed from the distilled juices of an unidentified Goblin Fruit.<br /> <br /> Well, the king is well past the emergency 4 hour mark and now he's experiencing the possible side effects. Namely, his constant, throbbing malehood. He's tried everything to make it go down, but it doesn't seem to work, and he can't possibly hold public appearances while he's in this state. So he's asked you to track down the manufacturers and see if there's any way to resolve the situation. Spring is just around the corner, and if the king shows his face at court while pitching a tent, he'll be laughing stock of the Freehold!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 09-14-2017, 01:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-14T06:36:09-07:00","id":1140148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1140086#post1140086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>76)</b> <b>Satyriasis</b><br /> <br /> The King of Spring has a sensitive, personal matter he's been requesting your motley's help with. Over the last couple of years, he's had trouble... performing, as it were. Not trusting mortal medicine to work on his supernatural physiology, he decided to hit up the Goblin Markets and see if they had anything that could restore his virility. It turns out they did, and within a few minutes, the King of Spring had his hands on a new form of male enhancement supplement brewed from the distilled juices of an unidentified Goblin Fruit.<br /> <br /> Well, the king is well past the emergency 4 hour mark and now he's experiencing the possible side effects. Namely, his constant, throbbing malehood. He's tried everything to make it go down, but it doesn't seem to work, and he can't possibly hold public appearances while he's in this state. So he's asked you to track down the manufacturers and see if there's any way to resolve the situation. Spring is just around the corner, and if the king shows his face at court while pitching a tent, he'll be laughing stock of the Freehold!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not to mention the BP problems he's definitely having. Changeling AMI, here we come!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T09:35:25-07:00","id":1140535,"title":"","content":"78. The Shattered Self: <br /> <br /> The Winter Queen has learned a fatal weakness of the Night Hermit, a Gentry known for its persistence in capturing or eradicating the Changelings who settle in a certain city. Before she could deliver this truth to her Court and the hungry blades of the Summer courtiers, she was caught by one of the Hermit's loyalists and slain. What the Hermit did not know, could not know, is that at the moment of her death she enacted an Oath with the Wyrd itself to deliver this message to her people. Instead of her essence lost, scattered to the labyrinth of ivy, it shattered and burst from the Hedge. By virtue of their connection to the Freehold, all who have been touched by the magic of the Winter Queen now has a shard of her essence within them, a small whorl of her memories and personality. Together they must unite the pieces through the dreamscape to reconstruct the memory of what she knows...but they should beware, all who were touched by the Queen's magic has a part of her, including the assassin who caught her in the first place, slaying all pieces they can find to protect their Keeper.<br /> <br /> 79. Premier:<br /> <br /> A new television show has been muscling its way onto the tvs in the PC's city. It always comes on late at night, often when someone is alone, and usually in the presence of Changelings. The show is always the same, a grainy still of a long corridor, dark with thorns. At the far end, the glint of black water can be seen slowly approaching the camera. In the Hedge around the city the dry, packed earth has begun to grow damp, marshy. The dreams of the mortals are filled with seascapes and skies that ripple and flow like the waves of the sea. Even the gentry attacks seem to have broken off, sometimes in the midst of their plans...the mortals they infect harvested of their glamour and left alone. Something is encroaching on the city through the Hedge, something beyond even the Gentry themselves...but what? How long until it arrives?<br /> <br /> 80. Gentrification<br /> <br /> There is an old legend in Detroit among the Lost that call it their home. They say the Hedge of the city is protected by a guardian Fey who shelters the escaped and spirits away their enemies for a Durance to burn away their darkness. Long has the Steel Crown Freehold maintained this legend and long have they benefited from the power of their mysterious benefactor. In the long time since their prosperity, Kings and Queens of seasons have risen and fallen, the truth of the legend lost like so many who come. But recently a Hound of Summer has come to Detroit and slain the guardian fey, too vengeful to accept its protection. Only then has the truth of its inception been revealed. Three titles, claimed by the Name-Taker Spear in battle against the gentry many years ago and bound to the Freehold of the Steel Crown. He or She who sits in the throne of Autumn inherits whichever titles remain, transformed into a Gentry to protect the Lost of Detroit. With no more guardian, the Titles are once again free to be claimed by the one who will take Autumn's seat next. Some vie for power, others for peace, and still others would see any dead who would see themselves transformed into the likes of their captors. What do the PC's do? Let it play out or join the fray?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7452-tulpa-theory","name":"Tulpa Theory","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T10:57:18-07:00","id":1140556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1140148#post1140148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not to mention the BP problems he's definitely having. Changeling AMI, here we come!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm not familiar with those abbreviations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>81) Black Fox</b><br /> <br /> Nobody thought it possible, but it happened. Somebody within the Freehold managed to <i>scare off </i>a team of Huntsmen that were pursuing them. I don't mean they found some sort of contract or clause that caused them to abandon the chase, either. Rumors are saying that the Huntsmen took one look at the guy, then turned and bolted their way back towards Arcadia like frightened children. Obviously, the first people to talk to would be the Autumn Court, but they claim to have no knowledge of anybody who could possibly do that within their organization. And whoever they are, they have yet to come forward and identify themselves to the rest of the Freehold. So who is this mysterious Changeling that can intimidate such single minded creatures like the Huntsmen, and why are they choosing to remain anonymous?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=9pUR9oxXDMA\" data-code=\"9pUR9oxXDMA\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/9pUR9oxXDMA/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T11:42:07-07:00","id":1140575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1140556#post1140556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I'm not familiar with those abbreviations. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>BP: Blood pressure<br /> <br /> AMI: Heart attack or Acute Myocardial Infarction","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-15T13:17:05-07:00","id":1140614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1140575#post1140575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> BP: Blood pressure<br /> <br /> AMI: Heart attack or Acute Myocardial Infarction</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Ah, I thought that's what BP might have stood for. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-09-30T07:20:11-07:00","id":1145518,"title":"","content":"<b>82)</b> Beauty cream that gives its users the flawless perfection of a Greek sculpture, technological developments that exceed their creator's expectations and run perfectly with little to no maintenance, toy collars that cause their wearers to act like literal animals. Somebody has found a way to harness the reality warping powers of the True Fae and is using them to alter the mortal world in a similar fashion. The big questions everybody's asking is <i>&quot;how, why, and can it be stopped?&quot;</i><br /> <br /> And if it can't be stopped... <i>&quot;can it be mass produced?&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T15:42:41-08:00","id":1172407,"title":"","content":"<b>83: Town of the Fae (Origin story)</b><br /> <br /> In a secluded village near a forest, all humans seem to have developed supernatural powers. Fae live in the woods and prey upon neighboring, mundane villages while your village acts as a safe-house for survivors, mostly young children. You play human orphans who are developing powers in the local, surprisingly large orphanage. The orphanage lends able children to the village as commonplace workforce in exchange for meat, grain and goods.<br /> One night, you spy the local amiable trader leading captured, wounded strangers into the woods. It is soon clear that there never were any neighboring villages - only a portal. The trader, the butcher, even the orphanage keeper - <i>all</i> grownups wear masks and they don't take in children out of the goodness of their hearts. They took you in to fatten you.<br /> This isn't a village. This is an Arcadian slaughter house.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13128,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","user":"Spinnerling","date":". 08-28-2018, 07:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-01T16:50:02-08:00","id":1172431,"title":"","content":"<b>84: Royal Pledges</b><br /> <br /> A Goblin Lord's magical crown has been stolen by a changeling, and he wants you to get it back - or else.<br /> After finding the culprit, it turns out the crown is on the Winter King's head. He had the crown stolen to magically block out his debt to the Gentry:<br /> The Gentry helped him to the Winter throne and now he must give them three changelings from the Freehold or suffer his life.<br /> You are left with three alternatives:<br /> <i>Shall the King give the Gentry their due, shall he keep the crown, or do you condemn him to death?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13128,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","user":"Spinnerling","date":". 08-28-2018, 07:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T17:24:25-07:00","id":1235115,"title":"","content":"<b>85:</b> <b>The Unwanted Child</b><br /> <br /> Last night, you had a sexual encounter with the woman of your dreams. She left almost immediately after, but this morning you found a basket on your doorstep with a newborn baby and a hastily written note pinned to the handle.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;They're your problem, now!<br /> <br /> P.S: Thanks for the good time!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Further investigation into this child reveals you are somehow its biological father. Even worse, the child appears to possess an unnatural longevity and will not age like a normal human. Clearly, this infant is chimerical in nature, and you have been saddled with the responsibility of raising it.<br /> <br /> Or have you? Maybe last night's experience was a hint as to how you can resolve this predicament?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T05:38:56-07:00","id":1239995,"title":"","content":"<b>86: Invitation to a Slaughter</b><br /> <br /> The Ashen Court's bargain is this: when Autumn reigns, the Gentry and their pawns must give clear warning before an attack. The more powerful the Gentry involved, the further in advance this warning must come, with the notice period usually varying from a few hours for the weakest of the Others to a lunar month for the strongest.<br /> <br /> So how does the Freehold react when, on the night of the Autumn coronation, a number of loyal servants of the Freehold are found slaughtered in the Hedge, their cooling corpses carved with a formal announcement of an attack scheduled precisely a year and a day from now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24314-itokro","name":"itokro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24314_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-29T09:10:21-07:00","id":1240077,"title":"","content":"<b>87: Cold War</b><br /> <br /> The Winter Court has done something unprecedented, they've decided to go on the offensive! Not openly, of course, that's never really been their style. But they have started to employ the use of covert operations and sabotage against the enemies of the Freehold. While some people are happy to see the Winter Court finally getting off their asses and doing something useful for a change, many others are growing very nervous. The Winter Court has always preferred the path of least resistance, remaining out of sight and out of mind. So who or what could possibly have convinced them to take a more proactive means of defending themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T02:30:00-07:00","id":1242664,"title":"","content":"<b>88: Her Darkest Hour (historical campaign - WW2 Britain)</b><br /> <br /> The legends say that King Arthur never truly died. That one day, at Britain's darkest hour, he will return to save his people. Now, with Nazi bombs pulverising the capital every night and the looming threat of full-scale invasion, plenty believe that darkest hour has come. As people increasingly remember the old legends, their desperate hopes are heard. Deep below the Somerset countryside, something is stirring.<br /> <br /> But Arthur is a king of myth, with very little historical basis. And anything that can sleep for 14 centuries before reawakening cannot be human. So just what kind of creature <i><b>is </b></i>the King-Under-The-Mountain? And what will happen if, or when, he emerges?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24314-itokro","name":"itokro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24314_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T07:51:19-07:00","id":1242717,"title":"","content":"<b>89: An Expanding Freehold</b><br /> <br /> A Changeling notorious for not taking up a Court but still pledging loyalty to the Freehold has vanished for a few days, and returned with an offer for the Freehold\u2019s leaders. They have gone into the Hedge and managed to make a Bargain with a strange entity, one that, at least inadvertantly, allowed them to escape Arcadia. Now they are the Monarch of an entirely new Court, and wish to join the Freehold and add to its diversity. The problem is the Freehold has gone by just fine without this new Court, and for all they know the new Court will muscle in on their already existing Changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T22:00:37-07:00","id":1243401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>itokro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1242664#post1242664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But Arthur is a king of myth, with very little historical basis. And anything that can sleep for 14 centuries before reawakening cannot be human. So just what kind of creature <i><b>is </b></i>the King-Under-The-Mountain? And what will happen if, or when, he emerges?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, he has '<b>dragon'</b> in his name, doesn't he? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------------------<br /> <br /> <b>90) The Prince and the Pauper</b><br /> <br /> A high ranking member of the court decided they wanted to escape their more tedious responsibilities for a time and has acquired a remarkably identical doppelganger to pose as them while they took some time off. After a few weeks, they decided to get back in the game, only to find that their imposter has no intention of stepping down from their position. In fact, it seems they've gone quite mad with power and are accusing the deposed noble of being the fake, instead!<br /> <br /> Desperate to avoid worsening the situation, they've reached out to you and your motley in the hopes that you can remove the doppelganger from office in a clean and precise manner. Preferably without anybody noticing they're gone, so that the actual prince can slip back in without invoking unwanted backlash from the public. While it may seem like a simple case of assassinating the imposter when nobody's looking, it would probably be a good idea to procure some evidence of their true identity, just in case something goes wrong!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T09:50:20-07:00","id":1243529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1243401#post1243401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, he has '<b>dragon'</b> in his name, doesn't he? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>A dragon made entirely of writing implements! Truly the most ferocious of foes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24314-itokro","name":"itokro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24314_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T20:49:19-07:00","id":1243697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>itokro</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1243529#post1243529\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A dragon made entirely of writing implements! Truly the most ferocious of foes!</div> </div> </div> </div>That's effectively my Changeling Luther Blackwell, though in his case his draconic elements are horns (ballpoint pens) and claws (fountain pen nibs), though his blood is ink as well. I always liked the name Pendragon, and wanted it to be literal here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 08-08-2018, 12:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T16:53:34-07:00","id":1244664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1243697#post1243697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's effectively my Changeling Luther Blackwell, though in his case his draconic elements are horns (ballpoint pens) and claws (fountain pen nibs), though his blood is ink as well. I always liked the name Pendragon, and wanted it to be literal here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Huh, Blackwell actually sounds like an awesome name for an ink dragon. Maybe their wings could be made out of quill feathers? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T23:39:34-07:00","id":1244735,"title":"","content":"<b>91) Unwanted Guests:</b><br /> <br /> The Spring Court decided to hold a surprise party to celebrate one of their senior members' contributions to the Freehold. Nothing too terrible about that, except that person in charge of organizing the event accidentally wrote <i>&quot;everyone's invited&quot;</i> on all the invitations. Now, the Huntsmen and even more importantly the True Fey have a written invitation to stroll right into the Freehold without having to bother with all the ritualistic formalities that normally ward them off!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T16:59:15-07:00","id":1249577,"title":"","content":"<b>92. Waking the Giant</b><br /> <br /> You are called to a human town on top of a hill in the middle of the forest to investigate disappearances. The rumor is that the Captain of the guard is not human, but something supernatural. You arrive during a town meeting and you can spot that under his mask, the Captain indeed is of the fae.<br /> You confront him in his house in the valley beneath the town, but he is not alone. There are bodies on the floor and the last sacrifice draws its final breath.<br /> The hill beneath the town opens its eyes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13128,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","user":"Spinnerling","date":". 08-28-2018, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T20:00:51-07:00","id":1249600,"title":"","content":"<b>93) A Christmas Story:</b><br /> <br /> Normally, the holidays are a time for celebration and merriment. But not for those who remember the origins of such holidays... Not for those who have been to the world of the Fae and seen its denizens with their own eyes. The weather has become especially fierce this time of year, and people have begun to go missing in the dead of night with no trace as to what's become of them. Mortal authorities are stumped trying to solve the case. This is the season when the Winter Court is supposed to assume leadership, but when the Freehold attempted to visit their court for guidance, they found the place turned inside out, and a single word gouged into the wall by inhuman claws...<br /> <br /> <i><b>&quot;KRAMPUS!&quot;</b></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-29T08:51:20-07:00","id":1249707,"title":"","content":"<b>94) The Eye of the Fae </b>(A scene for an origin story)<br /> <br /> A terrible crime has been committed in your village and a forest troll has been seen escaping the crime scene before turning into an unknown human guise.<br /> There is a Nordic myth that if you drill a hole through a stone and look through it, you will be able to see the true face of anything fae. You get one of these stones and call to a village meeting. When everyone gets there and their attention is on your friends, you take up the stone to search for the troll... only to see half of the citizens change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-04T14:32:01-07:00","id":1251494,"title":"","content":"<b>95) Today is Thanksgiving</b><br /> <br /> You start preparing a dinner for Thanksgiving and immediately you get sucked into the Hedge. All you have is a turkey-carving knife. Can you get out?<br /> <br /> Alternatively, play from the perspective of the people looking for you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24271-froggo","name":"Froggo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24271_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-11T11:24:04-07:00","id":1253327,"title":"","content":"<b>96) Son of Iron</b><br /> <br /> Some crazed Nam vet just walked out of the Hedge with his grandchildren in tow and the heads of a True Fae Syzygy still dripping with fresh ichor on his belt. Who is this guy!?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":7106,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","user":"Extant Reality","date":". 09-18-2018, 05:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7106-extant-reality","name":"Extant Reality","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7106_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"155"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-16T05:46:18-07:00","id":1254744,"title":"","content":"<b>97) Every Conceivable Outcome</b><br /> <br /> One of the True Fae has captured you in some kind of time loop in which you're forced to relive the same day over and over and over again. The only changes that occur throughout the day are the ones which you actively impose upon the scene. Without your interference, everything plays out identically to how it did when you first arrived here. You're not sure why, but it seems that one of the Fae has developed a fascination with exploring the boundaries of <i>'cause and effect'</i> and it seems you've been chosen as one of their test subjects!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T04:31:12-07:00","id":1255462,"title":"","content":"<b>98) Lambs to the Slaughter</b><br /> <br /> The sheep are plotting something, you just know it. You've always known they couldn't be trusted, every since you hacked, slashed and crawled your way back through the Hedge. You've caught them staring at you out of the corner of your eye when you pass by them, and their bleating coincidentally hushes whenever you're nearby. They know you're on to them, and tensions are brewing to see who is going to make the first move in an attempt to take the other side out.<br /> <br /> You know this is the case, but for some reason, nobody else in the Freehold will listen to you. In fact, they think you've gone quite MAD!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-05T02:48:41-07:00","id":1334054,"title":"","content":"<b>99) Mirror Twins (origin story)</b><br /> <br /> Early in your life, you met a strange person claiming to have seen your twin sibling hurt and in need of your help, but you didn't take the bait. You ran and found your twin safe and free, but shortly after, the twin died.<br /> Now, several years later, in the corner of you eye, you see your mirror image blink.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13128-spinnerling","name":"Spinnerling","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-05T15:06:10-07:00","id":1334109,"title":"","content":"<b>100) Out Of The Bottle</b><br /> <br /> A motley has come across rumors of a genie in a bottle making rounds, a being who can perform amazing favors and tasks at a single command. Houses have gone up, lives have been saved, and people have gotten out of poverty. Sadly it's a cautionary tale; for each good act done there is a cruel edge put to it; the homes are not to code and fail in dramatic ways, lives are saved but left in a bad state, and what riches are gained are made at the cost of sold household items and fake goods. Strangely enough, the deeds aren't done instantly - they're actually done by a single individual's hard work, and not solely from magic. One Changeling claims that it was another Changeling doing these deeds, but if that's the case why the cruelty? And why is the bottle such an integral part of the story if it's a Changeling doing the deeds?<br /> <br /> <b>100a)</b> It's a genie alright, a being bound to a bottle that been housing them for centuries. The being's magic isn't quite like a Changeling's, not based on Contracts but on Dread Powers, but they are fae enough a Changeling can make a deal. The question is, is the genie trustworthy enough to make a deal with?<br /> <br /> <b>100b</b> It's a Changeling alright, trapped in a devious Token by a Keeper with a wicked streak. The Token keeps the Changeling trapped in a gilded Hollow like space, unable to leave unless called for by the bottle's holder and unable to die by self-harm or neglect while within the bottle. Years of wishes and mistreatment has made the Changeling jaded and cruel, which begs the question: freeing the Changeling would be simple with some iron to the token, but is it wise to do so? Freeing the genie from the bottle is the right thing to do, but with such a dangerous personality free to do what they want is it worth the risk? Further, what if their Keeper is still around and learns their genie is no longer kept under wraps?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T15:04:24-07:00","id":1383676,"title":"","content":"<b>101) Firstborn of Fae</b><br /> <br /> The PC Motley have come across a man looking after a child clearly capable of utilising the Wyrd and faerie magic. When pressed, they learn that the man made a deal with one of the Gentry; in return for curing his sister of the innumerable cancers riddled throughout her body, the man would give the True Fae woman his firstborn child when they reached their eighteenth birthday. The real clincher is the identity, and nature, of the child\u2019s mother; the very member of the Gentry that the man made the deal with!<br /> <br /> How will the Motley react to this revelation? And how will the local courts take the news that one of the Others had a child with a human of all things!? And just which of the True Fae was it anyway?!?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-27T18:54:21-07:00","id":1384333,"title":"","content":"102) A group of artist types with some awareness of faeries have recently produced a piece of art that disrupts whatever fetches use to pretend to be human.<br /> The disguise is disrupted so much that regular humans can tell, but afterwards many decide that they had been dosed with some kind of drug.<br /> The problem is that the artists are keeping hold of it, because they don't want it to used for &quot;murderous&quot; purposes.<br /> \u25cf Uses the Wilde Society.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26055-krat05","name":"Krat05","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-13T19:43:36-07:00","id":1388214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1251494#post1251494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>95) Today is Thanksgiving</b><br /> <br /> You start preparing a dinner for Thanksgiving and immediately you get sucked into the Hedge. All you have is a turkey-carving knife. Can you get out?<br /> <br /> Alternatively, play from the perspective of the people looking for you.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Extant Reality</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5365-101-story-hooks?p=1253327#post1253327\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>96) Son of Iron</b><br /> <br /> Some crazed Nam vet just walked out of the Hedge with his grandchildren in tow and the heads of a True Fae Syzygy still dripping with fresh ichor on his belt. Who is this guy!?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh... now I'm wondering about how these to story hooks might be pieced together...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/22.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25791-terrorcooper","name":"TerrorCooper","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T13:41:54-07:00","id":1399365,"title":"","content":"103.<b>A Degenerate Beast</b><br /> A Dancer Beast that was once a major member of [Fill-In-The-Blank's] freehold, but now, a series of personal disasters has reduced the Feathered Firedancer's Clarity all the way down to 1. She has become dangerously unbalanced, and perceives everything through the lens of her experiences in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> Having murdered several mortals, the Feathered Firedancer must now be brought to heel. The Mask can only cover up so much, and now Huntsmen have been seen in the area.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 06-28-2020, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-29T10:06:47-07:00","id":1399874,"title":"","content":"104.<b>The Five Frweholds</b><br /> Not all changelings who escape from Arcadia have left with compassion intact. Some, in fact, emerge with all conscience scoured away by their Keepers' delicate cruelties.<br /> <br /> One such changeling was an Italian mobster. He thought he was a hardass, he thought he was tough, but Arcadia showed him how wrong he was.<br /> <br /> When he escaped, he just went right back to the life he once led. Gathering likeminded changelings around him, he helped build a Court based on La Cosa Nostra, called the Five Freeholds.<br /> <br /> A den of sociopaths and crooks, the Five Freeholds have muscled in on mortal organized crime, and now a gruesome gang war has broken out. Huntsmen have allied themselves with the mortal criminals, albeit covertly.<br /> <br /> Things are about to go BOOM!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-08-11T20:32:34-07:00","id":1407653,"title":"","content":"105. <b>The Ever-changing Goblin Queen </b>- Rumor has it that one of the Changelings in the Freehold visits a Goblin Queen every year. Several Courtiers are willing to pay handsomely if a Motely can figure out what they are up to.<ul><li><b>Possible Plot</b>: The Changeling was once a Goblin Queen and managed to return to being a Changeling by replacing themselves with a child. The Changeling was remorseful about what they had done and now every year helps the Goblin Queen find a replacement so they can go back to their human life. So far they have kidnapped 10 children, each one missing for one year only to come back to their families. Yes, the children lose some of their memories because of the Thorns, but they are still young and can recover. Or so the Changeling hopes...</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"211"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-08T07:00:14-08:00","id":1469913,"title":"","content":"106. You find out that your Fetch has started a cult whose view points are anti-technology. If that wasn't a problem already, a mysterious benefactor has been visiting them an supplying them with weapons and targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25291-donteatrawhagis","name":"DontEatRawHagis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25291_2.png","title":"Member","rank"